1
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:46,000
The Christmas Shoes is a drama, tv movie film directed by Andy Wolk.

2
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Two separate stories mesh - in the first, a young music teacher, Maggie Andrews, begins dying of a heart
condition and her son Nathan tries to get a pair of Christmas shoes for her before she dies.

3
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
In the second, lawyer Robert Layton and his wife Kate are slowly drifting apart and the matter
comes to a head during Christmas when Kate takes over for Maggie for the school choir.

4
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Robert Layton, played by Rob Lowe.

5
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Maggie Andrews, played by Kimberly Williams-Paisley.

6
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Nathan Andrews, played by Max Morrow.

7
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Kate Layton, played by Maria del Mar.

8
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Jack Andrews, played by Hugh Thompson.

9
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Dalton Gregory, played by Dorian Harewood.

10
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
The Christmas Shoes is a 2002 American-Canadian made-for-television drama film based on the song
and the novel of the same name which was broadcast on CBS on December 1, 2002.

11
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
It was shot in Halifax, Nova Scotia.

12
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
It is the first in a series of ten books by VanLiere and
the first movie made from the series.

13
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
There have been four additional movies made from the series, The Christmas Blessing (2005), The
Christmas Hope (2009), The Christmas Secret (2014) and The Christmas Note (2015).

14
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
The tone is emotional.
